# Changelog updates

Whenever you make a **notable** change to this repository (feature, fix, breaking change, docs that affect operators, new MCP tools, new agents/workflows/policies), update [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) in the same change set.

## Rules

1. Put new entries under `## [Unreleased]` until a version is tagged/released.
2. Use Keep a Changelog sections: `Added`, `Changed`, `Deprecated`, `Removed`, `Fixed`, `Security`.
3. Write concise bullets focused on **user/operator impact**, not every file touch.
4. Do **not** invent a version bump unless the user asks; keep work in `[Unreleased]`.
5. After a release/tag, move `[Unreleased]` items into a dated `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section and leave a fresh empty `[Unreleased]`.
6. Skip changelog for pure chores with no observable effect (typo-only in comments, local WIP renames) unless the user asks.

## Example

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added
- Short description of the new capability

### Fixed
- Short description of the bugfix
```
